{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A57LL4CHd5PU6ZTooKVdzE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# SunnyWake — Swift + SwiftUI 完整規格書\n2\t\n3\t> 給 7 歲兒童的「語音互動鬧鐘」。100% 離線、無廣告、無追蹤、宮崎駿手繪風。\n4\t> 本文件為 AI 開發助手（Claude / Cursor / Copilot）的系統提示與實作藍圖。\n5\t> 目標平台：iOS 17+（iPhone 主，iPad 相容）。\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 0. 為什麼是 Swift + SwiftUI（不是 Tauri）\n10\t\n11\t| 關鍵點 | 結論 |\n12\t|---|---|\n13\t| 鬧鐘背景排程 | iOS 只允許 `UNUserNotificationCenter`，Swift 直接呼叫；Tauri 要寫 bridge |\n14\t| 離線語音辨識 | Swift 內建 `SFSpeechRecognizer` + `requiresOnDeviceRecognition = true`，免下載 vosk model |\n15\t| 兒童類別審查 | Apple 偏好 native，webview 殼常被退件 |\n16\t| App size | 10–20 MB（Tauri + vosk model 50 MB+） |\n17\t| 開發時程 | MVP 約 2–3 週，Tauri 至少 4–6 週還要對抗工具鏈 |\n18\t\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t## 1. 環境準備\n22\t\n23\t### 系統與工具鏈\n24\t- **macOS**: Sonoma 以上\n25\t- **Xcode**: 15.x（含 Command Line Tools、iOS 17 SDK）\n26\t- **Apple Developer Program**: 必須（US$99/年，上架前付）\n27\t- **實機**: 建議準備一台 iPhone 真機測試麥克風與通知行為\n28\t\n29\t### 專案建立\n30\t```bash\n31\t# Xcode → File → New → Project → iOS → App\n32\t# Product Name: SunnyWake\n33\t# Interface: SwiftUI\n34\t# Language: Swift\n35\t# Storage: SwiftData（iOS 17+）\n36\t# Include Tests: ✅\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t### Info.plist 必填鍵\n40\t```xml\n41\t<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>\n42\t<string>鬧鐘需要聽你說「我起床了」才能關掉喔！聲音只留在這台 iPhone 裡，不會傳出去。</string>\n43\t\n44\t<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>\n45\t<string>用來聽懂你說的話，把鬧鐘關掉。所有辨識都在這台裝置上完成。</string>\n46\t\n47\t<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>\n48\t<array>\n49\t  <string>audio</string>\n50\t</array>\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\t### Capabilities（Xcode → Signing & Capabilities）\n54\t- Push Notifications：**不要**勾（會被誤判收集資料）\n55\t- Background Modes → Audio：✅（鬧鐘響時前景播音）\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## 2. 專案檔案結構\n60\t\n61\t```\n62\tSunnyWake/\n63\t├── SunnyWakeApp.swift            # @main 進入點\n64\t├── ContentView.swift              # Root NavigationStack\n65\t│\n66\t├── Models/\n67\t│   ├── Alarm.swift                # @Model class，SwiftData\n68\t│   ├── VoiceClip.swift            # 家長錄音檔 metadata\n69\t│   └── WakePhrase.swift           # 喚醒關鍵字（\"我起床了\" / \"好的\"）\n70\t│\n71\t├── Views/\n72\t│   ├── Home/\n73\t│   │   ├── HomeView.swift         # 主畫面：時間 + 龍貓 + 鬧鐘列表\n74\t│   │   └── CloudBackground.swift  # 飄動的雲朵背景\n75\t│   ├── Alarm/\n76\t│   │   ├── AlarmListView.swift    # 卡片列表\n77\t│   │   ├── AlarmRingView.swift    # 鬧鐘響起的全螢幕\n78\t│   │   └── RewardView.swift       # 成功關閉後的彩帶獎勵\n79\t│   ├── Settings/\n80\t│   │   ├── ParentalGateView.swift # 家長閘門\n81\t│   │   ├── AlarmEditorView.swift  # 新增/編輯鬧鐘\n82\t│   │   └── RecordingView.swift    # 錄音介面\n83\t│   └── Components/\n84\t│       ├── GhibliButton.swift     # 主要按鈕元件\n85\t│       ├── WatercolorCard.swift   # 水彩卡片\n86\t│       └── TotoroAvatar.swift     # 龍貓吉祥物（會眨眼睛）\n87\t│\n88\t├── Services/\n89\t│   ├── AlarmScheduler.swift       # UNUserNotificationCenter 包裝\n90\t│   ├── AudioRecorder.swift        # AVAudioRecorder\n91\t│   ├── AudioPlayer.swift          # AVAudioPlayer\n92\t│   ├── SpeechRecognizer.swift     # SFSpeechRecognizer (on-device)\n93\t│   └── PermissionManager.swift    # 集中要權限\n94\t│\n95\t├── Theme/\n96\t│   ├── GhibliColors.swift         # 色票\n97\t│   ├── GhibliFonts.swift          # 字型\n98\t│   ├── Animations.swift           # 雲朵飄動 / 樹葉搖擺\n99\t│   └── Sounds/\n100\t│       ├── totoro_breath.caf      # UI 互動音效（≤30s, 系統格式）"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf2951c0-7aa5-41b5-92a9-f15c57da5d6a","uuid":"fcfb3876-38e9-4ad7-b77e-b9ba0a2a8ad7","timestamp":"2026-05-31T16:57:59.859Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lion/Documents/SunnyWalker/docs/swift_native_spec.md","content":"# SunnyWake — Swift + SwiftUI 完整規格書\n\n> 給 7 歲兒童的「語音互動鬧鐘」。100% 離線、無廣告、無追蹤、宮崎駿手繪風。\n> 本文件為 AI 開發助手（Claude / Cursor / Copilot）的系統提示與實作藍圖。\n> 目標平台：iOS 17+（iPhone 主，iPad 相容）。\n\n---\n\n## 0. 為什麼是 Swift + SwiftUI（不是 Tauri）\n\n| 關鍵點 | 結論 |\n|---|---|\n| 鬧鐘背景排程 | iOS 只允許 `UNUserNotificationCenter`，Swift 直接呼叫；Tauri 要寫 bridge |\n| 離線語音辨識 | Swift 內建 `SFSpeechRecognizer` + `requiresOnDeviceRecognition = true`，免下載 vosk model |\n| 兒童類別審查 | Apple 偏好 native，webview 殼常被退件 |\n| App size | 10–20 MB（Tauri + vosk model 50 MB+） |\n| 開發時程 | MVP 約 2–3 週，Tauri 至少 4–6 週還要對抗工具鏈 |\n\n---\n\n## 1. 環境準備\n\n### 系統與工具鏈\n- **macOS**: Sonoma 以上\n- **Xcode**: 15.x（含 Command Line Tools、iOS 17 SDK）\n- **Apple Developer Program**: 必須（US$99/年，上架前付）\n- **實機**: 建議準備一台 iPhone 真機測試麥克風與通知行為\n\n### 專案建立\n```bash\n# Xcode → File → New → Project → iOS → App\n# Product Name: SunnyWake\n# Interface: SwiftUI\n# Language: Swift\n# Storage: SwiftData（iOS 17+）\n# Include Tests: ✅\n```\n\n### Info.plist 必填鍵\n```xml\n<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>\n<string>鬧鐘需要聽你說「我起床了」才能關掉喔！聲音只留在這台 iPhone 裡，不會傳出去。</string>\n\n<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>\n<string>用來聽懂你說的話，把鬧鐘關掉。所有辨識都在這台裝置上完成。</string>\n\n<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>\n<array>\n  <string>audio</string>\n</array>\n```\n\n### Capabilities（Xcode → Signing & Capabilities）\n- Push Notifications：**不要**勾（會被誤判收集資料）\n- Background Modes → Audio：✅（鬧鐘響時前景播音）\n\n---\n\n## 2. 專案檔案結構\n\n```\nSunnyWake/\n├── SunnyWakeApp.swift            # @main 進入點\n├── ContentView.swift              # Root NavigationStack\n│\n├── Models/\n│   ├── Alarm.swift                # @Model class，SwiftData\n│   ├── VoiceClip.swift            # 家長錄音檔 metadata\n│   └── WakePhrase.swift           # 喚醒關鍵字（\"我起床了\" / \"好的\"）\n│\n├── Views/\n│   ├── Home/\n│   │   ├── HomeView.swift         # 主畫面：時間 + 龍貓 + 鬧鐘列表\n│   │   └── CloudBackground.swift  # 飄動的雲朵背景\n│   ├── Alarm/\n│   │   ├── AlarmListView.swift    # 卡片列表\n│   │   ├── AlarmRingView.swift    # 鬧鐘響起的全螢幕\n│   │   └── RewardView.swift       # 成功關閉後的彩帶獎勵\n│   ├── Settings/\n│   │   ├── ParentalGateView.swift # 家長閘門\n│   │   ├── AlarmEditorView.swift  # 新增/編輯鬧鐘\n│   │   └── RecordingView.swift    # 錄音介面\n│   └── Components/\n│       ├── GhibliButton.swift     # 主要按鈕元件\n│       ├── WatercolorCard.swift   # 水彩卡片\n│       └── TotoroAvatar.swift     # 龍貓吉祥物（會眨眼睛）\n│\n├── Services/\n│   ├── AlarmScheduler.swift       # UNUserNotificationCenter 包裝\n│   ├── AudioRecorder.swift        # AVAudioRecorder\n│   ├── AudioPlayer.swift          # AVAudioPlayer\n│   ├── SpeechRecognizer.swift     # SFSpeechRecognizer (on-device)\n│   └── PermissionManager.swift    # 集中要權限\n│\n├── Theme/\n│   ├── GhibliColors.swift         # 色票\n│   ├── GhibliFonts.swift          # 字型\n│   ├── Animations.swift           # 雲朵飄動 / 樹葉搖擺\n│   └── Sounds/\n│       ├── totoro_breath.caf      # UI 互動音效（≤30s, 系統格式）","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":514}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Kbw3RNHJFWBJjz6f9wqiUE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a good understanding of the codebase and what needs to be done for Day 8. Let me now plan my work:\n\n**Day 8 Tasks:**\n1. **Modify `SunnyWalkerApp.swift`**: Add `pendingAlarmID: String?` property to `AppDelegate` and set it in `didReceive:withCompletionHandler:`\n\n2. **Modify `HomeView.swift`**: \n   - Add `.onAppear { checkPendingAlarm() }` \n   - Replace `.fullScreenCover(isPresented:)` with `.fullScreenCover(item: $firingAlarm)`\n   - Remove the long-press shortcut that was triggering the alarm manually\n\n3. **Modify `SunnyWalkerTests.swift`**: Replace the shallow notification tests with ones that actually test the AppDelegate's notification handling flow\n\nNow I'll start making these changes. First, I need to update the AppDelegate to store the pending alarm ID when the notification is received, then modify HomeView to check for that pending alarm on app launch and remove the debug gesture.\n\nFor the tests, the challenge is that `UNNotificationResponse` doesn't have a public initializer, so I'll need to find a way to create a testable notification response...\n\nActually, the cleanest approach is to extract the notification handling logic into a separate helper function on `AppDelegate` that I can test directly, rather than trying to construct a `UNNotificationResponse` in tests. That way I can verify the alarm-firing logic without dealing with the system's notification response object. and test a simpler helper that extracts the alarm ID from userInfo, rather than going through the full UNNotificationResponse path. The D reviewer said to test that \"if the `NotificationCenter.default.post(...)` line is removed from `didReceive:`, at least one test fails.\"\n\nSo the best approach is:\n1. Extract a `processNotificationPayload(userInfo: [AnyHashable: Any]) -> String?` method on AppDelegate\n2. Test THAT method (which returns the alarmID)\n3. Also test that calling this method and then checking pendingAlarmID gives the right result\n\nActually, let me re-read the D brief more carefully. They want me to instantiate `AppDelegate`, create a minimal mock `UNNotificationResponse` using a real `UNNotificationRequest` with `UNMutableNotificationContent`, call `didReceive:withCompletionHandler:`, and assert that `.alarmFired` is posted and `pendingAlarmID` is set. But here's the problem: `UNNotificationResponse` can't be instantiated directly, and I'm not sure how to construct it for testing without mocking frameworks.\n\nThe practical solution is to refactor the notification handling logic into a testable helper method that takes the userInfo dictionary directly, then test that method in isolation rather than trying to construct the full UNNotificationResponse object.\n\nBut wait—the requirements specifically ask for instantiating AppDelegate and creating a real UNNotificationResponse with UNNotificationRequest and UNMutableNotificationContent. That's more involved than the helper approach. Let me reconsider whether there's a way to construct UNNotificationResponse that I'm missing. Writing the refactored AppDelegate... Writing the alarm checking logic... Writing test methods...\n\nI'm also considering whether the `@MainActor` annotation is necessary here since `handleAlarmPayload` isn't marked with it, so it should be callable from any thread regardless.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the threading implications of `NotificationCenter.default.post` — it posts on the same thread it's called from, and if the observer is listening on the main queue, the callback gets dispatched asynchronously to the main thread. Since the test class itself might not be running on the main thread, I need to account for whether `waitForExpectations` will properly handle that async delivery.\n\nActually, `waitForExpectations` runs the run loop internally, so it should allow main queue callbacks to execute even if we're waiting from a background thread. But to keep things simple and avoid any threading edge cases, I'm considering whether to just add `@MainActor` to the test class or refactor away from `NotificationCenter` altogether.\n\nLet me simplify by using `queue: nil` for the observer, which makes the callback synchronous on the posting thread. This avoids any threading complications. Now I need to write out all the changes and double-check the AlarmRingView to see if the `alarm` parameter is optional.\n\nLooking back at the Day 5 notes, `AlarmRingView` has `var alarm: Alarm? = nil`, but when I pass a non-optional `Alarm` through `.fullScreenCover(item:)`, Swift will automatically wrap it as optional, so that should work fine.\n\nLet me check the actual initializer signature for `AlarmRingView` to confirm how it expects the alarm parameter.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4775,"cache_read_input_tokens":50245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4775,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf2951c0-7aa5-41b5-92a9-f15c57da5d6a","uuid":"2292f961-ed48-4c6c-ad9e-7640b99a8125","request_id":"req_011Cbb11ySdpdc7Em6APABmG"}
